# Acceptance Criteria — {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Scenarios

### AC-001 — Primary outcome (REQ-001)

- Given an authorised actor with valid input
- When the documented primary workflow is completed
- Then the intended outcome is produced atomically and is observable
- And failure does not leave contradictory state

### AC-002 — Boundary enforcement (REQ-002, REQ-006)

- Given unauthorised, malformed, replayed, or excessive input
- When it crosses a trust boundary
- Then it is rejected safely, recorded without secrets, and does not alter protected state

### AC-003 — Operability (REQ-003, REQ-004)

- Given a supported failure mode
- When operators follow the documented recovery action
- Then service is restored within the agreed objective and evidence is retained

### AC-004 — Architecture fitness (REQ-005)

- Given the dependency model
- When architecture validation runs
- Then domain policy has no dependency on delivery or infrastructure implementations

### AC-005 — Inclusive and performant delivery (REQ-007, REQ-008)

- Given a supported user channel and representative workload
- When accessibility and performance checks execute
- Then agreed targets pass with retained evidence

## Definition of accepted

Acceptance requires objective evidence, reviewer identity, execution context, and
date. A promise, screenshot without provenance, or unchecked box is not evidence.
